1
00:00:07,225 --> 00:00:10,025
Last time, we found three animal groups.

2
00:00:10,315 --> 00:00:12,325
Amphibians, birds and fish.

3
00:00:12,585 --> 00:00:13,885
Three more to go!

4
00:00:14,018 --> 00:00:15,498
An ant and a spider.

5
00:00:15,648 --> 00:00:17,368
Which one is the insect?

6
00:00:19,874 --> 00:00:21,474
It's You against the Buddies.

7
00:00:21,744 --> 00:00:23,054
You lock in first.

8
00:00:23,324 --> 00:00:25,144
One finger for every point.

9
00:00:25,424 --> 00:00:26,974
And a lizard is hiding.

10
00:00:27,264 --> 00:00:28,154
Find it!

11
00:00:29,472 --> 00:00:30,352
Round one.

12
00:00:30,672 --> 00:00:32,292
Which one is an insect?

13
00:00:32,582 --> 00:00:33,682
One, the ant.

14
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:35,042
Two, the spider.

15
00:00:35,362 --> 00:00:36,832
Show me with your fingers.

16
00:00:42,306 --> 00:00:43,286
Locked in!

17
00:00:43,414 --> 00:00:44,204
Two.

18
00:00:44,494 --> 00:00:46,364
It is tiny, and it crawls.

19
00:00:46,544 --> 00:00:47,714
Like a bug!

20
00:00:47,764 --> 00:00:48,394
One!

21
00:00:48,524 --> 00:00:49,404
The ant!

22
00:00:49,456 --> 00:00:50,176
One!

23
00:00:50,326 --> 00:00:51,576
But how do we know?

24
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,371
Are you ready?

25
00:00:57,811 --> 00:00:58,581
Three!

26
00:00:58,961 --> 00:00:59,621
Two!

27
00:00:59,991 --> 00:01:00,641
One!

28
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:01,781
Go!

29
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:04,170
Count with me!

30
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:06,760
One, two, three, four, five, six.

31
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:08,230
Six legs!

32
00:01:08,368 --> 00:01:09,938
Two feelers on its head.

33
00:01:10,208 --> 00:01:11,798
And three body parts.

34
00:01:12,311 --> 00:01:13,431
Now the spider.

35
00:01:13,781 --> 00:01:14,731
Eight legs!

36
00:01:15,001 --> 00:01:16,141
No feelers.

37
00:01:16,411 --> 00:01:17,651
Two body parts.

38
00:01:18,085 --> 00:01:19,645
The ant is the insect!

39
00:01:19,905 --> 00:01:21,335
The spider is not.

40
00:01:21,605 --> 00:01:23,345
It belongs to a different group.

41
00:01:24,155 --> 00:01:25,145
One finger?

42
00:01:25,465 --> 00:01:26,655
One finger up!

43
00:01:26,706 --> 00:01:27,356
Oops!

44
00:01:27,756 --> 00:01:29,016
Count the legs!

45
00:01:29,595 --> 00:01:30,895
Say it with me!

46
00:01:31,606 --> 00:01:34,696
Insects have six legs and a pair of feelers.

47
00:01:35,106 --> 00:01:39,786
The body of insects is divided into the head, thorax and abdomen.

48
00:01:47,318 --> 00:01:51,478
Insects have an outer covering that is usually hard and shell-like.

49
00:01:51,992 --> 00:01:54,822
Many adult insects have two pairs of wings.

50
00:01:55,102 --> 00:01:58,142
Some adult insects have only one pair of wings.

51
00:01:58,412 --> 00:02:00,172
Some do not have wings at all.

52
00:02:01,858 --> 00:02:02,558
My rule!

53
00:02:02,308 --> 00:02:04,688
If it has wings, it is an insect.

54
00:02:04,768 --> 00:02:05,688
A butterfly.

55
00:02:05,438 --> 00:02:06,758
A pigeon.

56
00:02:06,868 --> 00:02:08,078
Both insects!

57
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:09,910
Something is not right.

58
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:12,360
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

59
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,600
Hold on!

60
00:02:19,113 --> 00:02:20,243
Arms crossed?

61
00:02:20,503 --> 00:02:21,673
One finger up!

62
00:02:21,963 --> 00:02:23,483
A pigeon has feathers.

63
00:02:23,753 --> 00:02:24,843
It is a bird.

64
00:02:25,123 --> 00:02:26,943
Count the legs, not the wings!

65
00:02:27,301 --> 00:02:28,031
Oops.

66
00:02:28,111 --> 00:02:29,651
Six legs, not wings!

67
00:02:30,934 --> 00:02:31,934
Round two.

68
00:02:32,234 --> 00:02:33,454
A monitor lizard!

69
00:02:33,764 --> 00:02:35,654
Its skin is dry and scaly.

70
00:02:35,934 --> 00:02:36,824
Which group?

71
00:02:37,164 --> 00:02:38,514
One, amphibians.

72
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:40,124
Two, reptiles.

73
00:02:40,404 --> 00:02:41,524
Three, mammals.

74
00:02:41,804 --> 00:02:43,284
Show me with your fingers.

75
00:02:48,756 --> 00:02:49,736
Locked in!

76
00:02:49,864 --> 00:02:50,604
One!

77
00:02:50,714 --> 00:02:52,464
Four legs, like a frog.

78
00:02:52,517 --> 00:02:53,447
Two.

79
00:02:53,557 --> 00:02:55,677
Its skin is dry, not moist.

80
00:02:55,729 --> 00:02:56,349
Two!

81
00:02:56,519 --> 00:02:57,809
Lizards like me!

82
00:02:58,088 --> 00:02:59,398
The answer is two.

83
00:02:59,678 --> 00:03:00,858
Reptiles!

84
00:03:03,726 --> 00:03:04,756
Two fingers?

85
00:03:05,026 --> 00:03:06,246
One finger up!

86
00:03:06,294 --> 00:03:07,214
I knew it!

87
00:03:07,284 --> 00:03:08,474
I'm a reptile!

88
00:03:08,902 --> 00:03:11,882
Most reptiles, except snakes, have four legs.

89
00:03:12,163 --> 00:03:14,953
Reptiles usually have dry and scaly skin.

90
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,903
They breathe through their lungs.

91
00:03:17,193 --> 00:03:19,933
Most reptiles reproduce by laying eggs.

92
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:21,311
I hatched from an egg!

93
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:22,670
Be a scale!

94
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,940
Shrink down.

95
00:03:24,210 --> 00:03:25,150
Quietly.

96
00:03:27,435 --> 00:03:30,155
You are one scale on a monitor lizard's back.

97
00:03:30,595 --> 00:03:32,265
You are dry, and tough.

98
00:03:32,771 --> 00:03:33,871
Early morning.

99
00:03:34,311 --> 00:03:36,441
The air is cool, so you are cool.

100
00:03:36,871 --> 00:03:38,341
The lizard is slow.

101
00:03:38,784 --> 00:03:40,454
Now it crawls into the sun.

102
00:03:40,894 --> 00:03:42,394
Sunlight lands on you.

103
00:03:42,814 --> 00:03:43,884
You warm up!

104
00:03:44,695 --> 00:03:46,395
At noon, it is too hot.

105
00:03:46,875 --> 00:03:47,735
Splash!

106
00:03:48,195 --> 00:03:49,535
Into the cool lake.

107
00:03:49,995 --> 00:03:51,175
You cool down.

108
00:03:55,773 --> 00:03:56,923
Say it with me!

109
00:03:57,639 --> 00:04:00,189
Reptiles are cold-blooded animals.

110
00:04:00,609 --> 00:04:04,229
This means that they do not have a constant body temperature like

111
00:04:03,979 --> 00:04:04,779
humans.

112
00:04:05,039 --> 00:04:09,209
Their body temperature changes with the environment that they are in.

113
00:04:14,164 --> 00:04:16,864
Cold-blooded does not mean I am always cold.

114
00:04:17,074 --> 00:04:18,454
I warm up in the sun!

115
00:04:18,957 --> 00:04:20,417
Show me your score hand!

116
00:04:20,707 --> 00:04:21,737
More than two?

117
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:23,387
You beat the Buddies.

118
00:04:23,687 --> 00:04:24,747
Three fingers?

119
00:04:25,027 --> 00:04:26,037
High five!

120
00:04:26,684 --> 00:04:28,324
Did you spot the little lizard?

121
00:04:28,604 --> 00:04:30,134
It was on the lamp post.

122
00:04:30,404 --> 00:04:31,634
Is it a reptile?

123
00:04:31,904 --> 00:04:33,204
Tell someone at home.

124
00:04:33,932 --> 00:04:36,132
Let's read today's key words together!

125
00:04:36,422 --> 00:04:37,182
Ready?

126
00:04:37,519 --> 00:04:38,298
Insects.

127
00:04:39,772 --> 00:04:41,432
Head, thorax, abdomen.

128
00:04:43,469 --> 00:04:44,377
Reptiles.

129
00:04:46,024 --> 00:04:47,104
Cold-blooded.

130
00:04:48,644 --> 00:04:49,584
Well done!

131
00:04:50,681 --> 00:04:52,811
Next: this animal has wings.

132
00:04:53,081 --> 00:04:54,371
It flies at night.

133
00:04:54,651 --> 00:04:55,711
Is it a bird?

134
00:04:56,011 --> 00:04:57,591
Find out in Part Two!

135
00:04:59,256 --> 00:05:00,360
Say it with us!

136
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:01,910
Ready?

137
00:05:02,034 --> 00:05:02,694
One!

138
00:05:03,034 --> 00:05:03,734
two!

139
00:05:04,039 --> 00:05:05,214
Now you know!
